---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Identizen is built in the open by people who think the phone in your pocket is a better identity provider than a password database or a big-tech account."
>
  <article class="prose-idz max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Identity that belongs to the person holding it.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted">
      We are a small team with a specific complaint: every login on the internet is a shared secret,
      and every shared secret leaks.
    </p>

    <h2>What we believe</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>The phone is the identity.</strong> The key pair on the device is the user. It is never
        a code generator or a companion to something else.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The index is a phonebook, not a vault.</strong> Anything we host must be safe to leak.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Standard on the outside.</strong> Sites see OIDC. Browsers see WebAuthn. Nothing proprietary
        at the integration boundary.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>DX is the product.</strong> If integration takes more than five minutes, it is a bug.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Everything ships open.</strong> Apache-2.0. The enterprise tier is hosting, control, and
        support.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the company works</h2>
    <p>
      Identizen the company hosts the public index, the dashboard, and the docs, and sells the org
      tier: a hosted org index, fleet management, SSO bridging, audit, compliance packaging, and a
      support contract. Professional services cover migrations and custom adapters. The protocol,
      the app, the index, and the SDKs are one repository under one license, and self-hosters are
      first-class.
    </p>

    <h2>Governance</h2>
    <p>
      Benevolent dictator for now; a lightweight RFC process for spec changes once there are
      external implementers, plus a conformance suite so third-party indexes and apps can prove
      interop.
    </p>

    <p><a href={SITE.github} rel="noopener">The code</a> · <a href="/contact">Talk to us</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
